TAM-KNOX - A MULTI-REPOSITORY GIT WORKBENCH AND FILE VIEWER

tam-knox is a terminal multi-repository Git workbench and file viewer
for Tamlinux. It discovers Git repositories inside a folder, shows
their branch, dirty/clean state, changed files, and ahead/behind counts
with one-key remote sync, draws a commit history graph with commit and
diff inspection, provides a folder explorer with Git status badges, and
views any file in raw syntax-colored mode or rendered Markdown, HTML,
and Mermaid mode across tabs and split panes.

Follows the tam-idol 1.3.0 standard.


BUILD AND TRY

  Needs a C17 compiler, Make, and libtam 0.9.1 or later.
  LIBTAM_PREFIX defaults to $HOME/.local. The binary links libc and
  the static libtam archive.

    make
    make test
    make sanitize
    build/tam-knox
    build/tam-knox ~/Code/tamlinux
    build/tam-knox --status ~/Code/tamlinux
    build/tam-knox --graph .
    build/tam-knox --ascii --no-color .

  make install and make uninstall use PREFIX (default $HOME/.local).
  DESTDIR lets a packager stage the files. make clean removes build/.


KEYS

  Tab, Shift+Tab       Cycle focus across Sidebar and Main Workbench panes
  Up, Down, j, k       Move selection or scroll active view
  PageUp, PageDown     Scroll page up or down (also Space / b in viewer)
  Home, End            Jump to start or end of list or document
  Enter                Explore selected repo, expand folder, open file, or
                       inspect commit details and changed files
  Right                Explore selected repo (Repos), open closed folder or
                       open file in viewer (Explorer)
  Left                 Collapse open folder (Explorer), or return focus from
                       file viewer to Explorer tree
  Space                Stage or unstage file in Changes; page down in viewer
  Alt+1, Backspace     Switch left sidebar to Source Control (Repos/Changes;
                       Backspace returns from Explorer)
  Alt+2                Switch left sidebar to Explorer tree
  Alt+3                Open or focus the Git Graph tab
  Alt+B                Toggle left sidebar visibility
  f                    Fetch focused repository from remote (git fetch
                       --prune; non-destructive)
  s, Alt+S             Sync focused repository with remote (fetch, pull
                       --ff-only, push; confirms before main or test)
  Alt+A, F             Batch fetch all repositories with remotes (git fetch
                       --prune; non-destructive)
  Alt+C                Open commit message prompt for staged files
  c, Alt+K             Open Branch checkout & creation modal
  z, Alt+Z             Open Stash list management modal
  d, D, Alt+D          Toggle Side-by-Side Split Diff vs. Unified Diff
  Alt+E                Open current file in tam-edit ($VISUAL / $EDITOR)
  Alt+V, Alt+H         Split active main pane vertically or horizontally
  Alt+W                Cycle focus among split panes in active tab
  Alt+[ / Alt+]        Switch to previous or next workbench tab
  1-9, 0               Focus and select workbench tabs 1-10 in keyboard order
  R, Alt+R             Toggle Rendered vs. Raw syntax-colored file view
  B, Alt+F             Cycle branch filter in Git Graph (All / HEAD)
  Ctrl+F, /            Find in repo list, filter Explorer tree (live; Esc
                       clears), search commit graph, or find in file
  n, N                 Next or previous search match
  Ctrl+U               Update / refresh repositories, graph, and views
  Ctrl+N               Open a new workbench tab
  Ctrl+D               Close active split pane or tab
  Ctrl+C               Copy selection, commit hash, or path (OSC 52)
  Ctrl+E               Open command palette and one-handed chord composer
  g, Ctrl+G            Toggle keybinding guidance overlay
  Ctrl+Q, q            Quit tam-knox


WHERE THINGS ARE

  src/, include/   workbench TUI, Git engine, graph layout, explorer,
                   syntax highlighter, and Markdown/HTML/Mermaid viewer
  tests/           graph layout, Git operations, syntax, PTY, and CLI tests
  arch/            how the workbench and graph algorithm work
  keys/            keybinding specification (tam-idol standard)
  ideas/           surveys of VS Code, Git Graph, Emacs Magit, Lazygit,
                   Tig, and GitUI
  plans/           milestone plans
  bugs/, reviews/  numbered records
  work/            WHATNOW and work session records
  sandbox/         sample workspace and demo script
  ROADMAP.md       versions and milestones
  UPSTREAM.md      upstream code ledger
  COPYRIGHT        copyright and license notices


